c(20, "§5.2; §5.3 table (verbatim); §5.4 table (verbatim); §8.4; §8.5 E1, E2; §0.9 #7", "contradiction", "The paywall encounter, reconstructed from the 12 money-negative reviews (29.27%, 2.58, Wilson 17.6–44.5%): install believing it is free (listed Free, no limit stated) → set up habits and like it (9 of 12 volunteer praise) → hit the cap or a premium prompt and read it as 'the app is paid' → rate on the money, not the product; what would make someone pay, as inference (verbatim) " + table("## 5.3 What would make someone pay", 0) + " — barriers (verbatim) " + table("## 5.4 Upgrade barriers", 0) + " — the hypothesis: 'the people most likely to pay are the ones who got value free first. The current structure caps them early, at the point of setup, before the streak that creates the attachment has had time to form' — the two who call the free tier sufficient stayed, the only fair-price argument runs through free-tier satisfaction, and every 'everything is paid' reaction bounced within minutes; E1 gate features not habit count; E2 enforce the cap at day 14 rather than at setup; §0.9 #7 reconsider what the free tier gates", "cap at setup vs after attachment", "blocked-conversion", "money-negative 12 (29.27%) 2.58; 9/12 praise", "research", "hypothesis (n=1–3)", "generalisable", ["14095584857","12541530832","13250332545","13871805750"])
